{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along","id":1531355,"title":"Anarchs Unbound - The way Anarchs should have been all along?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-23T07:10:42-08:00","id":1531355,"title":"Anarchs Unbound - The way Anarchs should have been all along?","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> There's a lot of controversy in V5 over, well, everything so I thought I'd make a thread about going back in time to the supplement here. I did a WHERE I READ ABOUT IT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...chy-in-the-wod</a><br /> Which is about as deep a dive as you can get into it but I actually thought a more broad topic might be interesting.<br /> <br /> Basically:<br /> <br /> 1. Who are the Anarchs to you?<br /> <br /> 2. What should their role be in the setting?<br /> <br /> 3. What is their best portrayal and supplements dealing with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T08:53:53-08:00","id":1531361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along#post1531355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Who are the Anarchs to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because I've played for 30+ years, the Anarchs always seemed their realest to me when they were a blurry faction that was half-in, half-out of the Camarilla. The extreme cases were persona non grata but the majority could still be found in Elysium without raising too much of an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along#post1531355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What should their role be in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>The naysayers, the critics, the push to reform. And in some cases an allegory - The concept of a Baron is just a Prince by another name and I always like exploring how &quot;freedom fighters&quot; aren't always fighting for everyone's freedom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along#post1531355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. What is their best portrayal and supplements dealing with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Annabelle from LA By Night is one of the few people from that show that felt truly like an Anarch to me. And she is really a poster child for the movement. I say movement more than sect because I don't necessarily see it as a concrete sect the way the Camarilla and Sabbat are. Bookwise, I'll always have nostalgia regarding the Anarch's Cookbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T12:00:37-08:00","id":1531373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along#post1531355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folks,<br /> <br /> There's a lot of controversy in V5 over, well, everything so I thought I'd make a thread about going back in time to the supplement here. I did a WHERE I READ ABOUT IT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...chy-in-the-wod</a><br /> Which is about as deep a dive as you can get into it but I actually thought a more broad topic might be interesting.<br /> <br /> Basically:<br /> <br /> 1. Who are the Anarchs to you?<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are youngish Kindred rebelling against Mommy &amp; Daddy sire before enough time passes and they become the very thing they rebelled against.<br /> <br /> 2. What should their role be in the setting?<br /> <br /> As troublemakers in Camarilla domains that will get swatted when they become to annoying. On there own they would so many views at what there society should be is that they probably get into lots of infighting.<br /> <br /> 3. What is their best portrayal and supplements dealing with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I only have Anarchs Unbound and the most recent one plus and the Chicago By Night book that had a good take on them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T14:13:04-08:00","id":1531382,"title":"","content":"Here are some of my thoughts as someone whose always had affection for the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> 1. Somewhat recently I saw someone posit the idea that \u2018the Anarchs are all those vampires who actively resist the praxis of domains by the other predominant sects, clan broods, or even so-called barons\u2019. There\u2019s elements of the VtR Carthians in such a definition but I think that\u2019s potentially useful and to me it\u2019s helpful in both spreading a wide net while also offering a coherent definition. I think that presenting the Anarchs as a spectrum with a lineage connected to a heritage of rebellion and alternate forms would be very interesting - I would even note that, regardless of what vampires of certain generations may like to believe, the Camarilla itself in its earliest inceptions had elements of an anarch movement in comparison to what came prior.<br /> <br /> In a hypothetical \u2018Guide to the Anarchs\u2019 book with my fingers on the scale, I would want to include a history chapter which goes something like this: begin with fragments of Noddist mythology and folklore about the origins of vampiric rebels, then describe how for the majority of vampiric history the central authority in vampiric life was sire (and by extension, clan) and how in those periods \u2018anarch\u2019 would be a catch-all for any vampiric resistance to the domination of the sire (whether this involved destroying the sire to usurp them or joining the ranks of the earliest \u2018Caitiff\u2019 outlaws), a passage on how the rise of the great vampires and vampiric confederations saw the original forms of ideological Anarchs (for example, the Midnight Senate of Rome required vigilance against the underclass of vampiric childer who could gather in cosmopolitan cities and hypothetically make use of violence to press for their demands), the explosion of Anarchs with the fall of those old empires (in the European context) and the transition into the Dark Ages/War of Princes era we all know and love, the budding of Anarch tendencies within the high Middle Ages before the various catastrophes of the 14th &amp; 15th century unleashed chaos (Black Death, Inquisition, etc.) that would culminate in the (First) Great Anarch Revolt and from this event the formation-in-response of both the Camarilla and the Sabbat; following this would be the roles of Anarchs in modern history with more detail and the elaboration of the most significant Great Anarch Revolts from the first until the most recent revolts of the 19th &amp; 20th centuries.<br /> <br /> 2. The Anarchs should have a somewhat wide spectrum but imo they work better as the main default alternative to the Camarilla. IMO the default game style for introduction to VtM should focus on the Camarilla and Anarchs with the Sabbat, Independent Clans, etc. brought in to suit the development of player and storyteller experience and add complexity and greater possible narratives. It should be possible to have the classic anarch rebels and anarch sell-outs alongside a spectrum of different types. Having the main qualification being simply those seeking a different form of domain governance than the contemporary prince (and thus allowing everything from Chicago 2e style Anarchs who just want a somewhat better Camarilla Prince to fully fledged ideological Anarchs positing a significantly different system than the Camarilla. Anarchs should also help one to explore alternative methods of clan behavior and performance. From a setting perspective I feel that the Anarchs should have some territory of their own and some influential movements to make them a legitimate threat but I don\u2019t like the idea of the default being open war between the Camarilla and \u2018Anarchs\u2019 in general but rather that as one of several possible future plot threads.<br /> <br /> 3. I prefer the Anarch Cookbook and Anarchs Unbound (both for different reasons) over the Revised Guide to the Anarchs (the latter smacked to me of end-of-history/post-punk cynicism-as-realism). There are also gems to be found in Chicago by Night and LA by Night (although LA is significantly more rough). There are some good past threads about LA by Night that go into it more and how it could be revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T09:04:41-08:00","id":1531526,"title":"","content":"1) Anarchs are the ones loudest about putting the Punk into the Gothic-Punk World of Darkness: they are, in a nutshell, a profoundly necessary challenge to a callous Status Quo and simultaneously a perfect epitome of what made that Status Quo necessary in the first place.<br /> <br /> Life is never simple, so neither are the undead.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) Keeping the Camarilla honest - or at least keeping them from getting too complacent - without making the World of Darkness worse by their mere existence; making it plain that the Sabbat aren\u2019t just a rebellious counterculture, but something far more inhuman; generally providing the perfect stage on which players who like their vampires rowdy can play their Rock and Roll. <br /> <br /> Also, did I mention they put the \u2018Punk\u2019 in Gothic-Punk?<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Given that we have it on record that the Anarchs control New Zealand and that New York City\u2019s Anarchs have been banished to Staten Island, I vote WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS as a near-perfect evocation of the more low key \u2018We do what we like\u2019 Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll bet you cash money Lazlo Cravendale and Vlad the Poker would spend vacations going full MAD MAX WITH FANGS though (I suspect that Deacon would find it depressing to be just one of the Bad Boys, Nandor the Relentless prefers the quiet life, Nadja keeps getting kicked out for being too much of a Social Climber and Viago is exactly the sort of born-middle management who would assert praxis if only he thought it wouldn\u2019t get him murdered).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T13:49:29-08:00","id":1531540,"title":"","content":"Yes that is how I view the Anarchs myself Atticus as they keep the Camarilla on their toes and maybe some of the elders actually admire the rebel with a cause with a certain degree of amusement and bring back memories and passions that they once held before the weight of time started to push down on them. That said it's a fine line between amusement and becoming a unbearable annoyance and the older Anarch's also know this and maybe pick there battles with care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T10:24:28-08:00","id":1531688,"title":"","content":"1) They are either new Camarilla vampires who just couldn't take the repression, hypocrisy and divide that the sect enforces, or the old legacy of Anarchs who had to suffer the humiliation of the Thorns Treaty, even if it was supposed to be an equal sided peace signing, it turned into a &quot;bend the knee you ungrateful childe&quot;. In part, the Anarchs sued for peace in my eyes cuz they saw how the Anarch War was getting lots of people killed with the Inquisition coming down, so they wished to end the blood shed and sacrificed their ideals for peace.<br /> So the old Anarchs are kind of down, and the fresh blood really lifts their spirit, makes them want to fight and believe again. There are always sympathizers in the Camarilla, but the true Anarchs under the Anarch flag take off from Cam territory, trying to build their own society. Some, though, know that Camarilla and Sabbat will never leave them be (think all imperialistic nations), as such they take up arms and do go tear the ass-out of those sects, using their pride and pomp against them, infiltrating partisan style. <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) The Radicals, plain and simple. If you just want Autarkis left alone, political extremists, or just reformists, you can respectively make independent autarks, make 'em Sabbat, or have them be progressive Camarilla insiders who are trying and failing to make things better. If you go Anarch, you aren't a whining baby like many books and material shows, you are a radical fighting for a project. Now, which such project is what should make the Anarchs have very different factions (which the games tend to ignore completely). <br /> There simply isn't an Anarchist City in the setting, where everything is decided by assembly, where all leaders are elected and have no real authority, and all citizens work towards making unlife a little better doing their part, either watching the borders, organizing the others, looking out for the hungry and humanity-descending, and making sure the Herd is good. There is not even a hint of such a city existing, Anarchs are just either hungry-mobsters with a fake political speech or angry vamps vying for pure anarchy (not anarchism).<br /> They want to truly offer something different from the elder-repressors, the every vamp for themselves, the 'don't step in my domain or I will shoot you down', the 'I owe you whelp', and the whole 'you gotta be strong and submit to us cuz otherwise we will leave you dying in the streets'. <br /> <br /> <br /> 3) I've read many supplements, but all of them end up being sooo lacking, it always tells the same things, and end up making the Anarchs look totally directionless, dumb, critically hypocritical, liars and &quot;just as corrupt as The Man is&quot; (which is the most hegemonically-dominated narrative there is). By all accounts they should be in the right, even if full of dissension, in-fighting, unscrupulous violence, hardship, and truly hard decisions. But they always end up in that &quot;killmonger just murders his partners cuz his evil, invalidating all his point&quot; (and many other same examples), cuz anything else would be too radical (in both meaning lol), and actually make people think that bringing true change is the right thing to do. <br /> One book I did like (which honestly most Anarch supplements had some good things in 'em) is the MET Vampire the Masquerade (2013) book, in which there is the Anarch Status and positions, and plenty of them are purely public services and social collaboration, which in fact offers a different system and society from the Camarilla-Sabbat hierarchical, privative, and hostile systems. Under these Anarchs, I can't see a vampire being havenless, falling alone to the Beast, or getting desperate Hungry in the streets. <br /> <br /> <br /> A similar problem of portrayal and discourse wrestles with the Garou in Werewolf. There are many times when Pickard is wrong, and Magneto in in the right (when he is not a cartoon genocidal maniac). Sometimes rage is rightful and the source of it should be taken down, and something better should be put into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T15:04:46-08:00","id":1532062,"title":"","content":"My answers will be very generalist and home brewed.<br /> <br /> My tables tended to view the 4 big factions as a dual axis system. Camarilla as old Feudal lords vs Anarch rebellious youth.<br /> <br /> Sabbat fanatical cultists/Intel operation vs Inconnu age and anonymity. <br /> <br /> 1. Anarchs tend towards three camps: rebellious neonates/ancilla who think the grass is greener away from the Camarilla. They either believe The Cause(tm) and deluxe themselves into thinking it's impossible to become the evil they fight. Or after enough beatings and jyhad, settle into Cam or Sabbat turf.<br /> <br /> The other are Warlords who have Packs like Sabbat but minus the vinculum and Paths, and may roam or hold turf. They tend to keep nicer turf than a Sabbat pack but don't have the Intel apparatus because, surprise, Warlord Packs fight each other more than Sabbat Packs do. The outer enemy needs to be the bigger danger or they turn on themselves.<br /> <br /> The last is those who grow old and see little difference between Anarch and Camarilla and play both. Some may try with the Sabbath but the vinculum and Paths insulate it a bit.<br /> <br /> 2. Role in the setting? A playable representation of the Gini Coefficient writ large. Youngsters think they can Fite the Man(tm) with cellphones and utopian ideals. They may be a bit naive and view things in too human terms. Offer the players the chance to play but avoid the hypocrisy as they gain power. The machine is set to default to abuse the young.<br /> <br /> Or a Wild West setting where Packs of Coteries duke it out for turf and food. Who needs big stories or big bads when rival Anarchs want your shit?!?!?!? Dog eat dog. Until the Cam or Sabbat start manipulating and sticking their nose where is don't belong. Then the Packs unite! Right?...<br /> <br /> 3. We never leaned too much on source materials. We picked and chose at whatever was there and didn't seem corny. Most signature characters either were reskinned or died embarrassingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T17:05:49-08:00","id":1532213,"title":"","content":"Depends on the game. Most of the time, I use them as Shadowrunner types. In my universe, the Anarchs are too small and disorganized to really be called a &quot;Sect&quot;. They are mostly young vamps who have rejected being part of the establishment, and survive mostly because they do useful mercenary work. Either the Cammies or the Sabbat could crush them if they really thought it was worth the effort, but Anarchs just aren't worth bothering with. To give a recent example of how I use them: the Sabbat player pack in my game needed information on the New Orleans Camarilla. So they contacted some Setite Anarchs and bargained for it, basically using these Setite Anarchs the way Cammies use the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a small &quot;sect&quot; of mercenary trash is how I mostly use the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> There is ONE type of story I occasionally run in which the Anarchs are more prominent: I sometimes run what I call Near Empty World games. In Near Empty World games, the world vampire population is tiny. Like a few hundred world-wide tiny. In such world's being a kind of anarch is the default. The Camarilla is less a sect and more like a small conspiracy of old vampires who assassinate vampires who make too much noise. The players in these games mostly deal with the problems of being in a near empty world: humans finding out about them, their own beasts, that sort of thing, since there is no massive organization corrupting human society into preserving the masquerade. Instead, you are in a real risk of being found out by the mundane police, and have a small chance of being assassinated by the tiny &quot;Camarilla&quot; conspiracy if you really screw up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T20:50:01-08:00","id":1532227,"title":"","content":"Anarchs as covert operations for the Camarilla Prince I could totally see. Or at least ones that are pragmatic immortals who might ask for certain concussions as payment. Such as unique lore or decent feeding grounds or the right to embrace promising candidates. Yes Shadowrun was a favorite of mine when I was much younger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T13:50:25-08:00","id":1532256,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it I could see the older Anarchs becoming more mercenary in nature as they learn that Kindred society isn't going to change how it's run. With that in mind you could see them wanting to feather there nests so to speak and becoming like Mommy and Daddy sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T20:46:58-08:00","id":1532311,"title":"","content":"For me, the Anarchs represent the inevitability of Kindred society, and it's most understated curse. When the Antediluvians rose up and killed the Second Generation, Caine cursed them and their descendants. The clan curses were the most obvious form, but the other part of the curse is that children are destined to rise up, kill their elders, and then in time become the new elders who will be overthrown. When you get into mechanics (elders generally lose humanity over time, they develop the Thirst of Ancients and can only feed off of younger vampires, younger vampires power is capped and the only way for them to grow stronger is to diablarize the elders) coupled with aspects of the setting, like the fact that there are only so many positions of power in kindred society and there aren't going to be openings until someone dies, it makes it inevitable that the younger vampires will try to overthow the elders. This has always happened throughout history, the Anarchs are just the most recent form it.<br /> <br /> Any new system that the Anarchs make will inevitably mirror the one that currently exists. The current system of the Camarilla is largely the same one that existed during the Dark Ages, which was the same one that existed during the Roman era, which was the same as the one before it. There are a few small alterations here and there, but no matter the time period you have a single powerful vampire who takes over an area, and other vampires within that area have to do what he or she says. At most you might have a couple of elders who work together to some degree. But there's no room in the system for young vampires to hold power.<br /> <br /> Further, any new system the Anarchs try to introduce (whether a democratic voting system, a communist system, or whatever) this same basic idea of a single elder (or very small handful of elders) being in charge will end up happening again. Elders have higher stat caps so they really are stronger, smarter and wiser than vampires who are younger than they are (and that's not getting into ideas likesome Disciplines like Domination can't work on someone lower generation than you), and of course they're older so they've had more time to hoard power and make connections. This creates an inherently uneven playing field, and whatever system you end up with, the elders will inevitably rise to the top.<br /> <br /> So the Anarchs represent the unequal power of Kindred society, but also the fact that no matter how much they rage against it, they can't really change it. Vampires are monsters, and they don't get a &quot;happy ending.&quot; Anarchs are doomed to eventually become the elders that they hate. And many older elders are a bit indulgent of Anarchs, because they know what will happen in time and many of them used to be Anarchs when they were younger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T13:37:11-07:00","id":1532388,"title":"","content":"1: A deliberate mockery of civil rights and revolutionary movements<br /> <br /> 2: as little as possible, <br /> <br /> 3: ermmmm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T14:27:27-07:00","id":1532395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532388#post1532388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: A deliberate mockery of civil rights and revolutionary movements<br /> <br /> 2: as little as possible,<br /> <br /> 3: ermmmm</div> </div> </div> </div>Any rebels you'd actually think would be interesting as vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2024, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T16:26:11-07:00","id":1532399,"title":"","content":"1. I don't know if this will sound generic, it probably will, but they would be a group of ex-camarilla (or not) dissatisfied with their old place in the hierarchy, after all, despite having kindreds in the ivory tower, someone has to do the dirty work and/or risky, for a while it will, but no one wants to stay in that state forever, not to mention the privileges that allowed them to ignore certain rules, so they left when they could no longer tolerate it and that's why they founded their own group with their own vision and relatively less influential. It has a lot of variety of members, but we could divide them into three main categories: Those who want the best possible for the group, in this case Anarch; Those who desire influence and power that they couldn't obtain within the Camarilla; Those who just want to survive, very simplistic, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> 2. I think it could be used in a chronicle where they recently left the Camarilla and are still trying to stabilize and organize themselves; that comparison that within a more &quot;permissive&quot; group, it ends up generating possibly harmful internal factions, not that it doesn't happen in the Camarilla either, but in their case it's otherwise; To use the Camarilla as an antagonist without be Sabbat's vampire; Maybe play on hard; I've seen other ideas, but I think you can do them in Camarilla without any problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T16:31:44-07:00","id":1532400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532388#post1532388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2: as little as possible<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you were to avoid using that much, you would need a reason not to just take it off all at once.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T00:27:34-07:00","id":1532425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532395#post1532395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any rebels you'd actually think would be interesting as vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing revolutionary cells properly..... basically sit down with the Little Red Book, Anarchist cookbook, Stay Behind resistance manuals, insurgent tactics guides etc, add an ideology to it, with propaganda of the deed being a major driving force, a really loose structure, preferably of cells that don't know each other, and are infiltrated into the Camirilla, Sabbat, Cults or whoever holds local power, and start targeted killings and mass casualty events. (Bomb Elysium, assassinate the Sheriff/Templar, Thermite planted in Sabbat fire rituals to spice them up)<br /> <br /> Basically being Vampire Russian Imperial Movement or Comintern to contrast to the Sabbats vampire ISIS.<br /> <br /> Stop being rebels without a clue, and start being revolutionaries with bite, leave the wannabe gangsters, liberals with fangs and protestors as scapegoats, recruit any enraged survivors and remember, throwing bombs killed kings, it still works on Princes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T12:50:02-07:00","id":1532444,"title":"","content":"Except that Princes (Unlike Kings) actually <i>have</i> superpowers derived from their ancient bloodline and have almost certainly seen it all before - especially if they managed to outlive the 19th &amp; 20th centuries, with their abundance of insurgencies.<br /> <br /> Though admittedly good tactics ARE good tactics - I\u2019m more pointing out that it\u2019s dangerous to assume that the Establishment are not well aware of them (and preparing contingencies accordingly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Clarification 03-12-2024, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T12:56:12-07:00","id":1532446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532444#post1532444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Princes actually have superpowers derived from an ancient bloodline and have almost certainly seen it all before - especially if they managed to outlive the 19th &amp; 20th centuries, with their abundance of insurgencies.<br /> <br /> Though admittedly good tactics ARE good tactics - I\u2019m more pointing out that it\u2019s dangerous to assume that the Establishment are not well aware of them (and preparing contingencies accordingly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, not saying they would win, just that they would actually properly leverage the only advantage they really have, a better understanding of technology and culture.<br /> <br /> Seriously taking down Princes by what amounts to gang/militia tactics is amateur hour, and if is silly that it has ever worked. Which is also a problem the Sabbat can have, but at least they had more going for them.<br /> <br /> Basically embrace some people with a solid understanding of low intensity conflict and insurgent strategy, and go wild....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T13:12:11-07:00","id":1532448,"title":"","content":"In all fairness these tactics make Perfect sense \u2026 if you\u2019re willing to risk attracting the notice of Conventional authorities and allowing the Ivory Tower to suck Second Inquisition on you by proxy.<br /> <br /> Adopting straight-up terrorist tactics only works if, by a certain point, you WANT the world to see you at work: by contrast gangster tactics make it much easier for you to hush up your dirty work on a more long-term basis.<br /> <br /> Neither approach is faultless and both can have their uses: it\u2019s just that a wise Anarch knows when to forego the cutlass in favour of the stiletto (and vice-versa).\ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T13:40:22-07:00","id":1532450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532425#post1532425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doing revolutionary cells properly..... basically sit down with the Little Red Book, Anarchist cookbook, Stay Behind resistance manuals, insurgent tactics guides etc, add an ideology to it, with propaganda of the deed being a major driving force, a really loose structure, preferably of cells that don't know each other, and are infiltrated into the Camirilla, Sabbat, Cults or whoever holds local power, and start targeted killings and mass casualty events. (Bomb Elysium, assassinate the Sheriff/Templar, Thermite planted in Sabbat fire rituals to spice them up)<br /> <br /> Basically being Vampire Russian Imperial Movement or Comintern to contrast to the Sabbats vampire ISIS.<br /> <br /> Stop being rebels without a clue, and start being revolutionaries with bite, leave the wannabe gangsters, liberals with fangs and protestors as scapegoats, recruit any enraged survivors and remember, throwing bombs killed kings, it still works on Princes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of conversation, how about appealing to the thinbloods and Caitff? They tend to be cannon fodder so they could be the most willing to help, they would hardly have an important position, but bloodthirs would hardly be seen as a threat and Caitff are unpredictable so they can take good advantage of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T13:43:45-07:00","id":1532451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532446#post1532446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically embrace some people with a solid understanding of low intensity conflict and insurgent strategy, and go wild....</div> </div> </div> </div>Better just use a bloodbound in a already embraced kindred with actual experience in fight with a kindred, or make one of then become your ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T15:44:01-07:00","id":1532456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532451#post1532451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better just use a bloodbound in a already embraced kindred with actual experience in fight with a kindred, or make one of then become your ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but you would want to embrace the successful insurgent not to do the fighting, but to do the training and planning.<br /> <br /> Then use the standard disaffected and desperate as your foot troops and cut outs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T16:12:21-07:00","id":1532458,"title":"","content":"I actually like the character from Chicago by Night 5th Edition who seemed to be based on Call of Duty's protagonist, Duncan MacTavish. Basically, the Anarchs Embraced a REAL Special Operations commando and he becomes the boogeyman of the Camarilla in short order.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duncan_MacTavish\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duncan_MacTavish</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:17:34-07:00","id":1532464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532456#post1532456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could, but you would want to embrace the successful insurgent not to do the fighting, but to do the training and planning.<br /> <br /> Then use the standard disaffected and desperate as your foot troops and cut outs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but only the blood bond will guarantee his loyalty, otherwise you'll have to be lucky to find one of these and hope he doesn't turn you into a foot soldier. Kindred are cunning creatures and not everyone will see the embrace as a blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T06:33:17-07:00","id":1532495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532458#post1532458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the character from Chicago by Night 5th Edition who seemed to be based on Call of Duty's protagonist, Duncan MacTavish. Basically, the Anarchs Embraced a REAL Special Operations commando and he becomes the boogeyman of the Camarilla in short order.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duncan_MacTavish\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duncan_MacTavish</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I wonder how he stacks up against the \u201890s Special Forces archetype embraced by Clan Ventrue in time for their first Clanbook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T07:20:53-07:00","id":1532497,"title":"","content":"Despite my complete ignorance of how to translate from first edition CLANBOOK VENTRUE to 5th Edition, I\u2019ve looked up the canonical stats for the \u2018Military Man\u2019 archetype and for Duncan MacTavish:-<br /> <br /> <i>NOTE: The \u2018Military Man\u2019 seems to have been embraced at some point after the Invasion of Grenada in AD 1983 and the only stats we have for him are circa 1994 - if he survived the Sabbat \u2018Firedance\u2019 and other convulsions, he would have had three decades to acquire potency and pick up some new tricks, so this comparison can only be approximate</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - To start with, it\u2019s interesting to note that both these vampires seem to be of the 11th Generation (Though the character sheer for \u2018MM\u2019 says he has two dots in Generation and I\u2019m not sure what that indicates in this context - I don\u2019t actually own a MASQUERADE corebook at this point).<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Military Man has a Humanity of 7, MacTavish only 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> - MacTavish is ahead in physical stats: interestingly strength is dead level at 3, but the Gangrel Frank Castle has Dexterity 4, Stamina 5 Vs Ventrue Lt. Colonel Kilgore at 3 &amp; 4 respectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Military Man is, as might be expected, more of a people person: 3 dots each in Charisma &amp; Manipulation where MacTavish has only two in each.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Sergeant has much higher Wits (4 Vs 2) and slightly higher intelligence (3 Vs 2).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m not sure how to compare Self Control 3, Courage 5 and Conscience 2 against Composure 4 &amp; Resolve 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Willpower is 9 in both cases.<br /> <br /> <br /> - In terms of comparable skills, both have Brawl (Military Man 2/MacTavish 4), Drive (3 each), Firearms (3 Vs 5), Melee (1 Vs 4), Stealth (2 Vs 4), Investigation (3 each), Medicine (2 each) and Politics (1 each).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Otherwise the general impression is that the Military Man is exactly the sort of officer who could (and possibly should) be giving MacTavish orders; the former is clearly built more as a team player while the latter focuses on getting it all done singlehanded (For one thing the Military Man has Allies, Contacts and Resources, while the ex-sergeant seems to be more of a \u201c\u2026 in a CAVE, with a box of SCRAPS!\u201d sort of operator).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Finally, Disciplines are Fortitude 2 for each; the Military Man has Presence 1, MacTavish has Protean 4. <br /> <br /> <br /> So by the look of things this would be an interesting match, but the Military Man either needs to be leading a field team or substantially boosted after thirty extra years of being a vampire to stand a serious chance against MacTavish in head-to-head confrontation (Especially in hand-to-hand).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, he does seem to be rather better suited to doing things that aren\u2019t being a fairly typical Garth Ennis character, so there\u2019s that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T13:27:48-07:00","id":1532521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532450#post1532450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the sake of conversation, how about appealing to the thinbloods and Caitff? They tend to be cannon fodder so they could be the most willing to help, they would hardly have an important position, but bloodthirs would hardly be seen as a threat and Caitff are unpredictable so they can take good advantage of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work as a distraction to get the powers that be focus on these folks while the smart operators strike from a position that nobody would expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T13:29:54-07:00","id":1532522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532448#post1532448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In all fairness these tactics make Perfect sense \u2026 if you\u2019re willing to risk attracting the notice of Conventional authorities and allowing the Ivory Tower to suck Second Inquisition on you by proxy.<br /> <br /> Adopting straight-up terrorist tactics only works if, by a certain point, you WANT the world to see you at work: by contrast gangster tactics make it much easier for you to hush up your dirty work on a more long-term basis.<br /> <br /> Neither approach is faultless and both can have their uses: it\u2019s just that a wise Anarch knows when to forego the cutlass in favour of the stiletto (and vice-versa).\ud83d\ude42</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with the stealth strikes myself as you don't want to attract the attention of others who might pounce if they see a moment of weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T14:18:05-07:00","id":1532527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532522#post1532522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I go with the stealth strikes myself as you don't want to attract the attention of others who might pounce if they see a moment of weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the purpose of Anarchs is to establish a new state.<br /> <br /> Winning against the Camarilla means nothing when 90% of the Anarchs are fighting for personal booty like Domain and position not a greater cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T23:07:19-07:00","id":1532547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532448#post1532448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In all fairness these tactics make Perfect sense \u2026 if you\u2019re willing to risk attracting the notice of Conventional authorities and allowing the Ivory Tower to suck Second Inquisition on you by proxy.<br /> <br /> Adopting straight-up terrorist tactics only works if, by a certain point, you WANT the world to see you at work: by contrast gangster tactics make it much easier for you to hush up your dirty work on a more long-term basis.<br /> <br /> Neither approach is faultless and both can have their uses: it\u2019s just that a wise Anarch knows when to forego the cutlass in favour of the stiletto (and vice-versa).\ud83d\ude42</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were forsaking the cutlass for the stiletto, that would be one thing, but they aren't, targeted killings are a core strategy, and certainly could be made to look gang related, mass casualty events could be made to look like accidents (Disciplines make this easier) it's not maintenance of the Masquerade that's the problem, it's being a mockery of real movements, originally designed by a man who wanted the alt-right to kill their opponents, and those opponents to let them...and.yes MRH did say that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-14-2024, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T23:30:15-07:00","id":1532549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532527#post1532527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, the purpose of Anarchs is to establish a new state.<br /> <br /> Winning against the Camarilla means nothing when 90% of the Anarchs are fighting for personal booty like Domain and position not a greater cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Generally the Anarchs were pretty varied in their goals. Some were the hardcore ones who want to knock down the Camarilla. But a lot of Anarchs only called themselves that because they were unhappy with the local sect politics - if the Prince made some concessions, they'd move back into the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T10:24:11-07:00","id":1532585,"title":"","content":"That's why the Anarchs as much as I like them, will always wind up failing in the long run as outside of not liking what the other two groups offer are more likely to fight each other over what they think is the best way to go at running Kindred society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:16:23-07:00","id":1532610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532549#post1532549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it? Generally the Anarchs were pretty varied in their goals. Some were the hardcore ones who want to knock down the Camarilla. But a lot of Anarchs only called themselves that because they were unhappy with the local sect politics - if the Prince made some concessions, they'd move back into the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the Anarchs is strongly influenced by Juggler and Modius and them being the archetypal Anarch Baron (before it was a word) and Prince respectively.<br /> <br /> The two are a lot more similar than they are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T11:20:59-07:00","id":1532660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532425#post1532425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doing revolutionary cells properly..... basically sit down with the Little Red Book, Anarchist cookbook, Stay Behind resistance manuals, insurgent tactics guides etc, add an ideology to it, with propaganda of the deed being a major driving force, a really loose structure, preferably of cells that don't know each other, and are infiltrated into the Camirilla, Sabbat, Cults or whoever holds local power, and start targeted killings and mass casualty events. (Bomb Elysium, assassinate the Sheriff/Templar, Thermite planted in Sabbat fire rituals to spice them up)<br /> <br /> Basically being Vampire Russian Imperial Movement or Comintern to contrast to the Sabbats vampire ISIS.<br /> <br /> Stop being rebels without a clue, and start being revolutionaries with bite, leave the wannabe gangsters, liberals with fangs and protestors as scapegoats, recruit any enraged survivors and remember, throwing bombs killed kings, it still works on Princes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good for Anarchs, but...<br /> <br /> That's suffering from a general 'fighting the last war's fight' error.<br /> <br /> Problem is if that's the only strat the Anarchs have, they will fail due to it. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat are better at infiltration and can seduce Elders due to offering a cure to degrading Humanitas(the Paths) and or more loyal and unified in vision than the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Packs of shovelheads are more disposable and plentiful than Anarch gangs. Sabbat also has more consistent means of dealing with internal strife. <br /> <br /> Anarchs cant even define the freedom from the Camarilla they want(which can make them a different type of fun than a Sabbat game.)<br /> <br /> The problem with Anarchist Cookbook tactics is the 'day after'. Anarchs firebomb Elysium. Great! Now the Cam Elders will be leveraging the police and FBI to hunt down not just the perps, but also all the people associated with them. Shouldn't be too hard if they can access the ability to track cell phone use. <br /> <br /> And even if the local Elders cant flex the FBI, they will respond in kind: hire private mercs to infiltrate the Anarchs. Set a trap: hey Elders are gonna pinch the resources of the Anarch to anger them, then Cam will host one of their traditional events and allow the Anarchs to bomb that one as well. Anarchs show up but it was all a show and now they face organized combat vets that know not to outright fight them but to disrupt them in order to track their hidey-holes/havens as well as food supplies. <br /> <br /> Then, and decent Elder of the Cam won't kill the Anarch leaders outright, thats boring. They will catch each leader, Dominate/Entrance/Torture/Bond/use Thaumaturgy/or offer to turn coat, and release them back to the Anarchs to help it crumble from within. This not only defeats the Anarchs but discredits them as well. The Revolution(tm) turned out to be some campus ruffians who were mad they didn't understand power. Kids these days...<br /> <br /> And Anarchs are initially tied to their human connections moreso than Cam. Mainly due to recruiting. <br /> <br /> Plus, from a V5 narrative, are the Anarchs actually winning??? They are gaining turf, yes.<br /> <br /> But, <br /> <br /> Any good investor know when an investment t no longer runs or grows, it consolidates.<br /> <br /> There would be no move more Camarilla than giving up turf to the Anarchs just to let them ruin it and draw attention of human organizations as well as the Sabbat to themselves and away from the Cam. A Buffer State. The Cam can take it back in a few decades after the 'HUD Scam' runs it's lifespan and there is opportunity to expand power again for cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T13:44:07-07:00","id":1532665,"title":"","content":"My take is the Anarchs have massively benefited from the implosion of the Sabbat. For all the Sabbat's claims about being beyond the beast and being willing to do what the Anarchs are unwilling to do, that strategy ultimately destroyed the Sword of Caine. The Paths of Enlightenment work but they don't work WELL and only a handful of people who set out to learn them successfully do so.<br /> <br /> Plus, the remainder of the Sabbat Post-Civil War are all fanatically under the control of whoever wanted them to do the Gehenna Crusade to the point that they are all leaping into the mouths of the Ancients.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs decentralized system allowed them to survive that too.<br /> <br /> So all of the Sabbat's losses are the Anarch's games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T15:14:22-07:00","id":1532668,"title":"","content":"hmmmmm<br /> <br /> 1. No one really, they're quite underwritten lacking the deeper praxis (philisophical not vtm sense) they're ultimately a rather generic group of rebels which doesnt really work that well compared to other sects<br /> <br /> 2. they should be a fully realized faction by v5 with distinct idea's on how they're going to move forward. But they don't<br /> <br /> 3. probably anarch revised since it seems most aware of their limitations and integrates them as the 'left' of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T10:56:10-07:00","id":1532706,"title":"","content":"I still find it funny how the &quot;Second Anarch Revolt&quot; (which basically comes down to a super-duper weak and stupid Prince getting killed for the aforementioned reasons, and there not being a succeeding Prince or hard authority) is called as such, when the First one spanned over an entire century, over an entire continent, with hundreds to thousands of foci. And the repercussions of it left us with the modern Sects and vampire culture. <br /> <br /> The Free Anarch States were heavily underused, and the Great Leap Forward was (to me personally) a pretty dumb and empty plot. Camarilla didn't even react to the so called 2nd Anarch Revolt. <br /> <br /> I find it frustrating how the maniacs and genocidals of the Sabbat seem to be way more freedom-fighters and revolutionaries than any Anarch post-Thorns. The Anarchs by comparison are mostly juvenile rebels, one-time terrorist attackers, and fake grass-roots pop leaders. The damn (and practically non-existent other than one book) Council of Scales seem to do more common good to the Camarilla vamps than the Anarchs do to any Kindred at all.<br /> <br /> V5 making them more of an umbrella term, or a wide flag of independence was good. If you are not going to do a rebel-revolting faction right, than at least free it from such pretense. But still, it is not fulfilling half the potential it had and (now) has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:01:46-07:00","id":1532710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532549#post1532549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it? Generally the Anarchs were pretty varied in their goals. Some were the hardcore ones who want to knock down the Camarilla. But a lot of Anarchs only called themselves that because they were unhappy with the local sect politics - if the Prince made some concessions, they'd move back into the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see this happening with the older neonates and ancillea who starting to enjoy there creature comforts and become more mercenary in there outlooks.<br /> <br /> &quot; I will help you my Prince, but I want access to this particular region as my feeding grounds, the right to embrace this person or that you have some interesting items in your collection that I want to study.&quot; <br /> <br /> I bring that up as my coterie of 150+ kindred are very pragmatic in their dealings with the Camarilla, though they are Anarchs by default.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T14:06:01-07:00","id":1532723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532706#post1532706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it funny how the &quot;Second Anarch Revolt&quot; (which basically comes down to a super-duper weak and stupid Prince getting killed for the aforementioned reasons, and there not being a succeeding Prince or hard authority) is called as such, when the First one spanned over an entire century, over an entire continent, with hundreds to thousands of foci. And the repercussions of it left us with the modern Sects and vampire culture.<br /> <br /> The Free Anarch States were heavily underused, and the Great Leap Forward was (to me personally) a pretty dumb and empty plot. Camarilla didn't even react to the so called 2nd Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> I find it frustrating how the maniacs and genocidals of the Sabbat seem to be way more freedom-fighters and revolutionaries than any Anarch post-Thorns. The Anarchs by comparison are mostly juvenile rebels, one-time terrorist attackers, and fake grass-roots pop leaders. The damn (and practically non-existent other than one book) Council of Scales seem to do more common good to the Camarilla vamps than the Anarchs do to any Kindred at all.<br /> <br /> V5 making them more of an umbrella term, or a wide flag of independence was good. If you are not going to do a rebel-revolting faction right, than at least free it from such pretense. But still, it is not fulfilling half the potential it had and (now) has.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's extra weird because the French and American Revolution PLUS the Russian Revolution have all had massive amounts of Anarch Involvement added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T19:04:06-07:00","id":1532744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531355-anarchs-unbound-the-way-anarchs-should-have-been-all-along?p=1532706#post1532706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it funny how the &quot;Second Anarch Revolt&quot; (which basically comes down to a super-duper weak and stupid Prince getting killed for the aforementioned reasons, and there not being a succeeding Prince or hard authority) is called as such, when the First one spanned over an entire century, over an entire continent, with hundreds to thousands of foci. And the repercussions of it left us with the modern Sects and vampire culture.<br /> <br /> The Free Anarch States were heavily underused, and the Great Leap Forward was (to me personally) a pretty dumb and empty plot. Camarilla didn't even react to the so called 2nd Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> I find it frustrating how the maniacs and genocidals of the Sabbat seem to be way more freedom-fighters and revolutionaries than any Anarch post-Thorns. The Anarchs by comparison are mostly juvenile rebels, one-time terrorist attackers, and fake grass-roots pop leaders. The damn (and practically non-existent other than one book) Council of Scales seem to do more common good to the Camarilla vamps than the Anarchs do to any Kindred at all.<br /> <br /> V5 making them more of an umbrella term, or a wide flag of independence was good. If you are not going to do a rebel-revolting faction right, than at least free it from such pretense. But still, it is not fulfilling half the potential it had and (now) has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is that the Anarchs are intended for very small-scale stories. The player character gets abused by his sire, and joins up with other player characters who were abused by their sires, and they rebel against that tyranny. If you make them any bigger than that, they kind of break in terms of narrative purpose, because they then become just another version of The Man. 5th Edition doesn't seem to fully understand this, and so attempts to make them a sect, but almost immediately runs into the problem of trying to avoid making them The Man in the process. It tries to thread an impossibly tiny needle, and fails. It's like making Captain America President and then trying, somehow, to keep him as the antiestablishment guy fighting for freedom.<br /> <br /> I find it funny on a certain level; they knew they wanted the player characters to be rebels, which lead them to making Anarchs the default, but then immediately ran into the problem that if Anarchs are the default, then Anarchs become The Man in any story that lasts longer than four sessions, and therefore needs to flesh societal and bureaucratic issues out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T00:14:04-07:00","id":1536943,"title":"","content":"Anarchs, in my opinion, are just individuals who have been abused by and hate capital &quot;A&quot; Authority, in any form. Righteous or dishonorable, smart or dumb, or just pathetic edgelords, it's all the same impetus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}